  "about": "Central Park: Betamon's DDNA quest, shaped like the game's own partner quests (wstag375/wstag450 and the like). A fisher (character 43, image 6, the ones the stage's own DDNA givers use) shows up in the story window of the stage's own givers (special 0x24 = progress 14-38) and asks for the DDNA only while the party's levels add up to 45-74 (the same two thresholds as the stage's Patamon and Renamon givers). The request line re-enters the stage (warp) so the actors are made again, and then a river Digimon (its own sprite, sprites/river-digimon) appears while the request stands and the DDNA is not yours yet: talk -> event battle against MegaSeadramon (encounter betamon-pack:megaseadramon) -> talk again after winning -> the DDNA with the item-received signal (special 0x13). With the DDNA the fisher unlocks Betamon (special_conditions row give-betamon) and keeps it in the bag, like the originals.",
